From cce53bbb01a42bb099846ea862dfdbc78b8db201 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:03:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat(kms-worker): Profile H in the connector (lifecycle
 Level 1)

Off by default (profile_h.enabled = false): the same code path and no new
RPC.

- H5 / V7: after a denial, ask isAccountRetired for the check's subjects.
  If one is retired, the denial is final at its first attempt and typed
  account_retired (403, not retryable), so a later governance lapse cannot
  revive the request. Allowed requests pay nothing.
- H6 (opt-in): refuse users with regular code on the legacy path, which
  verifies signatures by ECDSA only.
- H2 / H8: the RFC-016 signature check runs through the Profile H policy of
  user-decryption-signature (code-first at one block, bounded ERC-1271
  budget and caps) in off, shadow or enforce mode, with per-request H4
  attempt state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
